    "description": "The Trinity is not a theological puzzle to be solved but the living God to be known and worshipped. Christianity is not merely monotheism with extra steps — it is the confession of a God who is eternally and irreducibly Triune: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit, one God in three persons. This course makes the doctrine of the Trinity both intellectually credible and doxologically compelling. Students will move from definition to defence to doxology — learning to state the doctrine clearly, distinguish it from its distortions, trace its footprints through redemption, and live out of its logic in worship, prayer, and community.",
