            "heading": "7. Summary",
            "html": "<div class=\"detail-table-wrap\"><table class=\"detail-table\"><thead><tr><th>Term/Concept</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One essence, three persons</td><td>One divine nature (<em>ousia</em>); three distinct subsistences (<em>hypostases</em>)</td></tr><tr><td>Sabellianism / modalism</td><td>One person appearing in three modes — condemned because the persons genuinely interact</td></tr><tr><td>Arianism</td><td>The Son is a created, lesser being — condemned by Nicaea (325 AD)</td></tr><tr><td>Tritheism</td><td>Three separate Gods — condemned because Scripture is uniformly monotheistic</td></tr><tr><td>Homoousios</td><td>&quot;Of the same substance&quot; — the Son is equal in essence to the Father</td></tr><tr><td>Perichoresis</td><td>The mutual indwelling of Father, Son, and Spirit in one undivided essence</td></tr><tr><td>Trinity and salvation</td><td>Father plans, Son accomplishes, Spirit applies — redemption is Trinitarian end to end</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
            "plainText": "| Term/Concept | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| One essence, three persons | One divine nature (ousia); three distinct subsistences (hypostases) |\n| Sabellianism / modalism | One person appearing in three modes — condemned because the persons genuinely interact |\n| Arianism | The Son is a created, lesser being — condemned by Nicaea (325 AD) |\n| Tritheism | Three separate Gods — condemned because Scripture is uniformly monotheistic |\n| Homoousios | \"Of the same substance\" — the Son is equal in essence to the Father |\n| Perichoresis | The mutual indwelling of Father, Son, and Spirit in one undivided essence |\n| Trinity and salvation | Father plans, Son accomplishes, Spirit applies — redemption is Trinitarian end to end |"
